<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Software Testing Guide</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #edfaf5;
            padding: 25px;
        }
        .container {
            max-width: 850px;
            margin: auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 25px;
            border-radius: 16px;
        }
        h1 { text-align: center; color: #167b5d; }
        .test {
            background: #e8f8f1;
            padding: 18px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            border-radius: 12px;
        }
        h2 { color: #167b5d; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
    <h1>🧪 Software Testing Guide</h1>

    <div class="test">
        <h2>Unit Testing</h2>
        <p>Checks individual functions or small parts of a program.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="test">
        <h2>Integration Testing</h2>
        <p>Checks whether different software components work together correctly.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="test">
        <h2>System Testing</h2>
        <p>Tests the complete application as a whole.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="test">
        <h2>Acceptance Testing</h2>
        <p>Checks whether the software meets user or business requirements.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="test">
        <h2>Why Is Testing Important?</h2>
        <p>Testing helps find defects, improve reliability and check that software behaves as expected.</p>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
